### 2. Run the Verification Checklist
Once the workflow processes the input, review the output at each stage against this checklist to ensure all nodes are functioning correctly:

- [ ] **Script Strategy Planner**: Did it return a specific narrative structure with justification? Is the word count target calculated? Does the retention schedule show specific timestamps?
- [ ] **Hook Writer**: Are there three distinct hook types, each with a hook science evaluation table? Is the recommended hook specific and platform-appropriate?
- [ ] **Script Body Writer**: Is it written in spoken language? Are `[VISUAL NOTE]`, `[PAUSE]`, and `[EMPHASIS]` cues present? Are section headers included with energy levels? Do the factual claims match the research?
- [ ] **CTA & Retention Layer**: Do the open loops have a plant, reference, and resolution with exact scripted lines? Are three CTA versions present?
- [ ] *(If testing Arabic Mode)* **Egyptian Dialect Layer**: Did it rewrite every spoken line? Are there any MSA verb conjugations? Is the Dialect score ≥ 8 before the loop exits?
- [ ] **Script Refinement**: Did it assemble all parts into one continuous document? Is the word count calculated?
- [ ] **Quality Loop**: Did Grade A exit the loop successfully? Did Grades B/C trigger a revision?
- [ ] **Final Package**: Was the B-Roll Shot List extracted from all `[VISUAL NOTE]` markers? Is the INTEGRATION DATA block present for upstream workflows?

If you want to specifically test the **Arabic Dialect Authenticity Layer**, you should run a separate test where you change `"scriptLanguage"` to `"Arabic (Egyptian)"` and provide `"dialectRegister"` (e.g., "Cairene media-standard") and `"codeSwitchingLevel"` (e.g., "Light").